# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file and shows a "Cite this repository"
# button; Zenodo reads it when minting a DOI.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Interpretable Machine Learning for Predicting GHS Chemical Hazard
  Classifications
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying dataset, please cite both this
  repository and the associated article once it is published.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sareer
    family-names: Ahmad
    alias: sareer555            # GitHub username
    email: sareerkh9194@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2580-091X'
    affiliation: Department of Chemistry, University of Peshawar
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sareer555/ghs-hazard-classification'
url: 'https://github.com/sareer555/ghs-hazard-classification'
abstract: >-
  A multi-label machine learning framework that predicts all nine Globally
  Harmonized System hazard pictograms from molecular structure. Trained on
  243,323 compounds whose classifications were reconciled across five
  regulatory sources, evaluated under a Bemis-Murcko scaffold split, and
  interpreted with SHAP. Includes a browser-based screening application and a
  command-line tool.
keywords:
  - GHS classification
  - multi-label learning
  - molecular descriptors
  - SHAP interpretability
  - chemical safety
  - scaffold splitting
  - QSAR
